# The same kernel at a two-block vocabulary: LLVM unrolls the first
# pass and turns the two-trip second pass into a predicate phi
# (`mov.pred` set true before the loop, copied in the header, set false
# in the latch). The matcher reads that as two trips. The default values
# Triton moves into loads it then issues unguarded are unused (no SASS in
# the kernel's ncu record) and count in no total: the loop's 261
# instructions per iteration, at most 960 per thread.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/gluon/ce_chunk_kernel.v8192.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/gluon/ce_chunk_kernel.v8192.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
CHECK: loop gluon_ce.py:54 ($L__BB0_3)
CHECK: instructions = 261
CHECK: AI(global) = 5.78125 flop/B
CHECK: totals [static]:
CHECK: instructions = <= 960
CHECK: unknowns: none
CHECK: coverage: loop_trips_resolved 100.0% (1/1)
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_3:                              // =>This Inner Loop Header: Depth=1 // loop: trips 2 | global per CTA: requested 32,768 B, unique ? | warp * × lane * | exec 1,024/CTA{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	mov.u32 %r340, 0x0; // unused{{$}}
